# Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in your own
# EmailJS values so a new-barber signup notifies the admin by email.
#
# EmailJS (https://www.emailjs.com) sends the email directly from the
# visitor's browser - no backend, no Firebase paid plan, no credit card.
# Free tier: 200 emails/month.
#
# Setup (one-time, free account):
# 1. Sign up at emailjs.com.
# 2. Email Services -> Add New Service -> connect your own Gmail (or any
#    inbox) -> copy the "Service ID".
# 3. Email Templates -> Create New Template. Set "To email" to
#    {{to_email}} and use {{shop_name}}, {{barber_email}}, {{barber_phone}}
#    in the subject/body -> copy the "Template ID".
# 4. Account -> General -> copy the "Public Key".
# 5. Put the three values below. When deploying, set the same three
#    variables in your hosting provider's environment settings.
#
# If these are left empty, shop signups still work (the request still
# goes into "pending" and shows up in the admin panel) - you just won't
# get an email and will need to check the admin panel manually.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
